        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.12,
            0.882,
            0.16
          ],
          "content": "**Check if replacing subtraction by addition in this way does not change the value of the expression, by taking different examples.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.174,
            0.556,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Let us take the numbers. 18 and 10 18 – 10 = 8 and 18 + (– 10) = 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.231,
            0.883,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "？ **Can you explain why subtracting a number is the same as adding its inverse, using the Token Model of integers that we saw in the Class 6 textbook of mathematics?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.304,
            0.698,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Refer chapter 10 of class VI Mathematics Textbook."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.337,
            0.882,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": "**Does changing the order in which the terms are added give different values? Ans:** No, For example, 14 + 10 +( – 5) = 19 or (– 5) + 10 + 14 = 19"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.425,
            0.24,
            0.444
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 29"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.457,
            0.882,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "？ **Will this also hold when there are terms having negative numbers as well? Take some more expressions and check. Ans:** Yes, For example: (– 4) + (– 2) = – 6 or (– 2) + (– 4) = – 6 (– 6) + (– 8) = – 14 or (– 8) + (– 6) = – 14 Write some more examples."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
